---
const costs = [
  {
    front: '$2k-$15k / month',
    label: 'Support-heavy flow',
    back: [
      ['Misread as', 'ticket volume.'],
      ['Paid by', 'Support + Product.'],
      ['If ignored', 'the same missing scaffold keeps returning as "user confusion."'],
    ],
  },
  {
    front: '$10k-$75k / month',
    label: 'Repeated onboarding drag',
    back: [
      ['Misread as', 'slow activation.'],
      ['Paid by', 'Onboarding + Implementation.'],
      ['If ignored', 'every new user must be re-taught what the product failed to sequence.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    front: 'Bad data',
    label: 'Weak intake scaffold',
    back: [
      ['Misread as', 'low-quality leads.'],
      ['Paid by', 'Sales + Qualification.'],
      ['If ignored', 'the form keeps inviting the wrong answer before anyone can qualify the case.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    front: 'Retention drag',
    label: 'Decision flow without action logic',
    back: [
      ['Misread as', 'low engagement.'],
      ['Paid by', 'Customer Success + Leadership.'],
      ['If ignored', 'users keep seeing information without knowing what to do next.'],
    ],
  },
];
---

<section id="cost" class="section-focus">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">Cost of not acting</p>
    <div class="section-heading-row">
      <h2>The cost is already being paid somewhere.</h2>
      <p>These are decision signals, not promises. The question is whether the recurring cost of not diagnosing the flow is already higher than the review.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card-row">
      {costs.map((cost) => (
        <button class="metric-reveal-card" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="metric-front">
            <strong>{cost.front}</strong>
            <em>{cost.label}</em>
          </span>
          <span class="metric-back">
            {cost.back.map(([term, detail]) => (
              <span>
                <strong>{term}:</strong> {detail}
              </span>
            ))}
          </span>
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.metric-reveal-card').forEach((card) => {
    card.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const expanded = card.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      card.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
    });
  });
</script>
